  "articles": [
    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "4. de after expressions of location\n\nNote the use of the particle de in the following sentence from Situation 3:\n\nSoko de Marunouchi-sen ni norikaete kudasai.\nThere transfer to the Marunouchi line.\n\nAn expression of location like soko 'there' followed by the particle de indicates the place where something has happened or will happen. This de is often equivalent to English 'at' or 'in', though the exact translation will depend, as here, on the context. You will see this particle again in later lessons."
    }
  ],
